Recommends: krb5-user
Description: PowerShell cmdlets for Samba Active Directory administration
 Provides the Active Directory cmdlets Windows administrators know, such as
 Get-ADUser, Get-ADComputer, Get-ADGroup and Get-ADObject, on Linux, so a Samba
 domain can be administered from a terminal without a Windows workstation.
 .
 The cmdlets are a PowerShell module backed by a Python process that reads the
 directory over LDAP, encrypted and authenticated with the caller's Kerberos
 ticket. Nothing but Samba's own LDAP server is needed on the domain controller.
